.TH SDE-VIEW 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-view \- Photo, the SDE image viewer and editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-view
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURI\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Photo views and edits one image at a time. It is the default application
for image files on the SDE desktop. Organizing a photo library (albums,
favorites, slideshows, import from cameras, batch actions on many photos)
is the job of Gallery,
.BR sde-gallery (1);
Photo's
.B Show in Gallery
(Ctrl+G) selects the photo there and F5 plays a slideshow of its folder in
Gallery.
.PP
Photo opens quickly: the preview embedded in a camera photo (or its cached
thumbnail) is shown at once, then a screen-sized image, then the full
image. Photos are shown upright following their EXIF orientation.
Animated GIFs play.
.PP
Photo steps through the other pictures of the folder (in name order), or
through a Gallery album (see
.BR \-\-album ),
with the arrow keys and a filmstrip below the photo.
.SS Viewing
The mouse wheel (or Ctrl+wheel for finer steps) zooms around the pointer;
drag to move a zoomed photo; double-click switches between best fit and a
closer look. Best Fit, Actual Size (1:1) and Fill Window are in the View
menu; full screen is F11.
.SS Information
The information panel (I) shows the file name, folder, size, type,
dimensions and colour profile, and the camera details from EXIF: date
taken, camera, lens, exposure time, aperture, ISO, focal length, flash and
exposure bias. Photos with a GPS position show the coordinates and an
.B Open in Map
link to openstreetmap.org.
.SS Editing
The edit panel (E) has four tabs. Edits are previewed and kept until
saved, and every step can be undone and redone.
.TP
.B Adjust
Exposure, brightness, contrast, saturation, warmth, fade and vignette.
.TP
.B Filters
Vivid, Warm, Cool, B&W, Noir, Sepia, Vintage, Matte and Invert, with a
strength.
.TP
.B Crop
Rotate (R, Shift+R), flip (H, V), crop with free or fixed aspect ratios
(C) and resize.
.TP
.B Draw
(D) Annotate the photo: a pen with smooth strokes, a highlighter (a
translucent marker that darkens what it covers, like ink on paper), an
eraser that removes drawn strokes but never the photo, lines, arrows,
rectangles and ellipses (outlined or filled), text (Sans, Serif or Mono,
any size and colour, with an optional background box), blur and pixelate
regions to hide private details such as faces, card numbers or
addresses, and a colour picker that takes a colour from the photo. A
palette and a custom colour, the stroke width and the opacity apply to new
drawings and to the selected one. The select tool picks a drawing to move
it, resize it by its corners (Shift keeps the proportions) or delete it;
double-click text to change it. Each stroke or shape is one undo step.
.PP
Drawings are kept in the coordinates of the full-size photo, so they stay
in place while zooming and panning, and they turn with the photo when it
is rotated or flipped. They stay a separate, editable layer until the
photo is saved; saving flattens them into the image at full resolution.
.SS Saving
Save replaces the file after asking; Save As writes a copy (JPEG, PNG,
WebP or TIFF). A JPEG that was only rotated or flipped is saved without
loss of quality by updating its EXIF orientation. Other edits, drawings
included, are encoded again with the chosen quality; JPEG files keep their
camera details (EXIF). GIF and SVG pictures are saved as PNG.
.SS Other actions
Copy Image (the clipboard offers PNG data, the file and its path), Set as
Wallpaper, Print (through CUPS
.BR lp ),
Open With another application, Show in Files
.RB ( liria ),
Show in Gallery and Move to Trash (freedesktop.org Trash). Changes are
announced to a running Gallery, which updates at once.
.SS Collages
File \(-> New Collage (Ctrl+N), Gallery's Create Collage and
.B \-\-collage
open the collage editor: any number of photos in ten designs (Grid,
Mosaic, Featured, Prints, Film Strip, Magazine, Shapes, Story, Panorama,
Framed) that adapt to the number of photos, with sizes from a square post
to 4K and A4, spacing, corners, borders, a colour or blurred background
and a title. Photos are moved and zoomed in their frames, swapped by
dragging one onto another and reordered; Export writes JPEG or PNG.
.SS Plugins
Tools \(-> Plugins switches the built-in plugins on and off: Collage, Auto
Enhance (Adjust tab), Frames & Borders, Watermark, Red-Eye Fix and
Background Blur (the Effects tab), Sizes for the Web and Social Media
(Sizes in the Crop tab) and Metadata & Privacy (All Details, Remove
Location and Save a Copy Without Details in the information panel, without
encoding the photo again). Action plugins, small
.I .plugin
files, run a program on the photo from the Tools menu. See
.I /usr/share/doc/sde/PHOTO.md
for details.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-album= ID
Step through a Gallery album, in Gallery's sort order:
.BR all ,
.BR favorites ,
.BR recent ,
.BR screenshots ,
.BI folder: PATH
(a library folder and its subfolders; a bare absolute path means the
same),
.BI device: PATH
(removable media),
.BI dir: PATH
(one folder) or
.BI list: FILE
(one path per line; Gallery's own albums are such lists).
.TP
.BI \-\-sort= ORDER
.BR newest ,
.B oldest
or
.BR name .
.TP
.B \-\-draw
Open the drawing tools (the Draw tab) once the photo is loaded.
.TP
.B \-\-slideshow
Play a slideshow of the photo's folder in Gallery.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start in full screen.
.TP
.B \-\-collage
Make a collage of the files (folders add the pictures in them).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.PP
With several files, Photo steps through exactly those files.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Left, Right, Home, End, Space, Backspace
Previous, next, first, last photo.
.TP
.B + \- 0 1 F
Zoom in, zoom out, best fit, actual size, fill.
.TP
.B R, Shift+R, H, V, C, E, D
Rotate right or left, flip, crop, edit panel, draw.
.TP
.B Draw tab: S, P, M, X, L, A, U, O, T, K
Select, pen, highlighter, eraser, line, arrow, rectangle, ellipse, text,
pick a colour. Shift while drawing gives 45\(de lines, squares and
circles; the middle mouse button moves a zoomed photo; Delete removes the
selected drawing; Esc deselects.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S
Undo, redo, save, save as.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+G, Ctrl+P, Delete
Copy image, show in Gallery, print, move to the Trash.
.TP
.B I, B, F1, F5, F11, Esc, Ctrl+W
Information, filmstrip, shortcuts, slideshow in Gallery, full screen,
leave, close.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Section
.B [photo]
keeps
.B jpeg_quality=
(default 92),
.B info=
and
.BR filmstrip= ,
and the drawing options
.BR draw_color= ,
.BR draw_fill= ,
.BR draw_font= ,
.B draw_text_size=
and
.BR draw_text_box= .
Set as Wallpaper writes
.B wallpaper=
in
.BR [appearance] .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-gallery (1),
.BR liria (1),
.BR sde-settings (1)
